analysis(rust): parser-backed shadow facts for seam-callee defeat (#3727 slice A) (#3739)

* feat(analysis): parser-backed shadow facts for seam-callee defeat (#3727 slice A)

The wrapper-seam and guarded-match shadow scans relied on byte-level
lexical scanners over masked bodies. This slice adds parser-produced
body facts and routes both shadow consumers through one flag-law
authority:

- FunctionFact/TestFact gain nested_fn_names and let_bindings
  (LetBindingFact { line, name }), produced by an ast::Fn/ast::LetStmt
  descent in the rust-analyzer summarizer (ra.rs) and left empty by the
  lexical fallback (parser-only, mirroring probe_shapes).
- extract/shadow.rs gains the fact twins (fact_body_defines_callee_fn,
  fact_body_let_shadow_line, extract_pattern_words) and ShadowAuthority:
  parser-backed files decide from facts; fallback files (or files absent
  from the index) run the byte scanners byte-identically. THE FLAG, not
  set emptiness, is the discriminator.
- Both consumers switch: the SeamCalleeCall relation
  (classify/related_tests.rs) reads the test's fact fields when the file
  is parser-backed, and the guarded Result match scanner gains
  guarded_result_match_scan_with_shadow_authority driven by
  extract_parser_oracles.
- FILE_FACT_CACHE_SCHEMA_VERSION 1.7 -> 1.8: warm pre-extension caches
  cannot serve parser-backed files without the fact fields (the flag law
  would read them as real no-shadow).

Zero classification drift: scanner-equivalent semantics at line
granularity; goldens check passes untouched.

* fix(analysis): close the synthetic shadow-fact wrapper and share the scan's coordinate base (#3739 review)

The wrapper in shadow_facts_for_body_text opened 'fn ... {' but never
closed it, so SourceFile::parse reported errors on every harness body and
the fail-closed branch returned empty facts — parser-backed harness
subjects then read 'no shadow' and a closure-local binding could
impersonate the wrapper seam's callee (devin h0fZ1, codex h6Z9y, gemini
h6ZRp, coderabbit h6cfM). The wrapper is now a complete fn item with the
closing brace on its own line, leaving every body-relative offset intact.

The parser facts fed to guarded_result_match_scan_with_shadow_authority
used the fn-keyword line as their coordinate base while the scan's
use-site offset counts 0-based lines from the top of function_text
(attributes included). With attribute lines above the fn, a let AFTER a
guarded match could suppress that earlier oracle (coderabbit h6cfG); the
facts now share the scan text's base, matching what the lexical scanner
over the same text decides.

Regression tests: body_text_wrapper_produces_non_empty_facts_for_harness_
bodies and parser_path_shadow_facts_share_the_scan_text_coordinate_base —
both verified to fail against the pre-fix code.

* fix(analysis): bump classified-seam cache generations for parser-backed shadow facts (#3739 review)

The shadow-authority flag law changes classified-seam content on
parser-backed files, but the PR only bumped the file-fact generation.
The classified-seam cache loads BEFORE any file-fact rebuild — a warm hit
returns classified seams without re-reading a single file — so a warm
1.11 envelope would serve pre-#3727 shadow classification indefinitely
(codex h6Z9w). The outer generation moves 1.11 -> 1.12, the sharded
0.17 -> 0.18, and the compact 0.18 -> 0.19, following the same semantic
transition pattern as every prior classification change.

Tests: the version-pin test documents the new generations, and
classified_generation_before_parser_backed_shadow_facts_is_a_miss seeds
an envelope under the pre-#3727 generation with identical identity
fields and proves the current key misses. The RIPR-SPEC-0175 policy
impact records the classified-generation law.

* test(analysis): make the shadow flag-law fixture reach the captured-call gate (#3739 review)

The SHADOWING_TEST_SOURCE fixture used a bare read ('let r =
try_parse_summary;'), which extract_call_facts never records as a call —
the three flag-law tests passed vacuously, before either shadow authority
ran (coderabbit h6ce-). The binding now initializes a closure and the
fixture invokes it, so the exact-name call gate is reached and both the
parser-backed and lexical authorities must defeat the admit.

Also: extract_pattern_words clones and clears the accumulator instead of
mem::take, keeping its capacity across words (gemini h6ZRu, output
identical); docs/specs/README.md regains its '# Specs' header with the
intended RIPR-SPEC-0175 index-row update moved to the actual index entry
instead of prepended above the header (gemini h6ZRv, coderabbit h6cfV).